      "id": "el1061",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 900,
      "width": 254.8,
      "height": 178.75,
      "text": "Asking an LLM to compute DPI is\nslower, pricier and LESS accurate\nthan four lines of Python.\n\nAsking Python whether a logo looks\n'too close to the edge to be\ndeliberate' does not work at all.\n\nKnowing which is which, and being\nable to say why, is the thing worth\ndemonstrating.",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Asking an LLM to compute DPI is\nslower, pricier and LESS accurate\nthan four lines of Python.\n\nAsking Python whether a logo looks\n'too close to the edge to be\ndeliberate' does not work at all.\n\nKnowing which is which, and being\nable to say why, is the thing worth\ndemonstrating.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
